---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Button from '../components/Button.astro';

const mechanisms = [
  {
    h: 'Isolation',
    p: 'Every task runs in a disposable, Podman-backed pod — its own filesystem, process space, and network egress. Pods are created on demand and destroyed on teardown; nothing persists between runs unless you mount it.',
  },
  {
    h: 'Injection',
    p: 'The pod never holds a vendor secret. It carries an opaque, revocable handle; the broker resolves that handle to the real credential and sets the authorization header on the wire, then proxies upstream. The raw key exists only on the broker→provider hop.',
  },
  {
    h: 'Redaction',
    p: 'On the same egress path the broker scans outbound request bodies and replaces stray secrets — cloud keys, tokens, private keys — with «redacted:poddle». An agent can’t exfiltrate a secret it read from your repo into a prompt.',
  },
];

const attacker = [
  { ok: true, t: 'An opaque handle', d: 'revocable in one call and worthless anywhere but your broker.' },
  { ok: true, t: 'A scoped, disposable pod', d: 'no long-lived vendor keys on disk, in env, or in memory.' },
  { ok: false, t: 'Your real provider key', d: 'it is never materialized inside the pod — only injected at the egress boundary.' },
  { ok: false, t: 'Secrets in the prompt body', d: 'scrubbed to «redacted:poddle» before they leave the broker.' },
];

const compliance = [
  ['SOC 2 & ISO 27001', 'On our roadmap — the broker is built as a single, hardened, audited control plane to make certification a matter of evidence, not re-architecture.'],
  ['DORA & EU AI Act', 'Per-user policy, revocable credentials, and a complete action trail map to the operational-resilience and traceability controls these frameworks require.'],
  ['Data residency', 'Pods run on your own cloud or self-hosted compute, in the region you choose. The broker holds credentials in a sealed vault; your prompts and code stay on infrastructure you control.'],
];
---
<Base
  title="Security - poddle"
  description="How poddle keeps vendor secrets out of every pod: isolation, credential injection at the egress boundary, and outbound secret redaction — with a full audit trail."
>
  <section class="container sec-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Security</p>
    <h1 class="sec-title">Built so the secret never lands in the pod.</h1>
    <p class="sec-lead">
      poddle gives a coding agent everything it needs to be productive and nothing it can leak. The
      raw credential lives in the broker; the pod carries a revocable handle. If a pod is compromised,
      there is no vendor key to steal.
    </p>
    <div class="sec-cta">
      <Button href="/docs" variant="primary">Get started</Button>
      <Button href="/#how-it-works" variant="ghost">See the flow</Button>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="container sec-body">
    <div class="sec-block">
      <h2>Three lines of defense</h2>
      <div class="mech">
        {mechanisms.map((m) => (
          <div class="mech__card">
            <h3>{m.h}</h3>
            <p>{m.p}</p>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-block">
      <h2>What a request actually does</h2>
      <ol class="flow">
        <li>The agent calls its provider as usual — <code>ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL</code> points at the broker, and <code>ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN</code> is a <code>poddle_…</code> handle, not a key.</li>
        <li>The broker gateway resolves the handle to the real credential in its sealed vault, strips the handle, and sets the real authorization header.</li>
        <li>It scans the request body and redacts any stray secrets to <code>«redacted:poddle»</code>.</li>
        <li>It reverse-proxies to the true upstream. The provider sees valid auth and a clean body; the pod never saw the key.</li>
      </ol>
      <p class="sec-note">The real secret is present on the broker→provider hop only — that is unavoidable, since the provider must authenticate you. What poddle guarantees is that it is never materialized inside the pod and never rides in a body it shouldn’t.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-block">
      <h2>If a pod is compromised</h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">A malicious dependency, a prompt-injected agent, a leaked pod — here is exactly what it gets:</p>
      <ul class="attacker">
        {attacker.map((a) => (
          <li class:list={['att', a.ok ? 'att--ok' : 'att--no']}>
            <span class="att__t">{a.t}</span>
            <span class="att__d">{a.d}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-block">
      <h2>Identity &amp; audit</h2>
      <p class="sec-sub">
        Every pod is created under a real identity, and every action — who spun up what, which
        credential was used, and when — ties back to a person, not a shared token. Credentials are
        revocable at the broker in one call, so offboarding a teammate or rotating a key is immediate.
        Share a live pod and each driver still works through their own identity, keeping attribution
        per-person.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-block">
      <h2>Compliance &amp; residency</h2>
      <dl class="compliance">
        {compliance.map(([h, d]) => (
          <div class="compliance__row">
            <dt>{h}</dt>
            <dd>{d}</dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="sec-block sec-disclosure">
      <h2>Responsible disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Found something? Email <a href="mailto:security@datadir.co">security@datadir.co</a>. We
        acknowledge reports within two business days, credit reporters who want it, and will not take
        legal action against good-faith research. Please give us a reasonable window to ship a fix
        before public disclosure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .sec-hero { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 4.5rem) 0.5rem; }
  .sec-title { font-size: var(--fs-hero); max-width: 18ch; margin: 1rem 0 0; }
  .sec-lead { font-size: var(--fs-lead); color: var(--muted); max-width: 60ch; margin: 1.2rem 0 0; }
  .sec-cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.8rem; margin-top: 1.8rem; }
  .sec-body { padding-bottom: var(--space-section); }

  .sec-block { margin-top: 3rem; max-width: 68ch; }
  .sec-block > h2 { font-family: var(--font-serif); font-weight: 400; font-size: 1.9rem; margin: 0 0 1.1rem; }
  .sec-sub { color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 1rem; line-height: 1.55; }
  .sec-note { color: var(--faint); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.55; margin-top: 1rem; border-left: 2px solid var(--border); padding-left: 1rem; }

  .mech { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 1.2rem; }
  .mech__card { border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; background: #fff; padding: 1.3rem 1.3rem 1.4rem; }
  .mech__card h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; color: var(--ink); }
  .mech__card p { color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; margin: 0; }

  .flow { margin: 0; padding-left: 1.3rem; color: var(--ink); line-height: 1.6; }
  .flow li { margin: 0.5rem 0; padding-left: 0.3rem; }

  .attacker { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.7rem; }
  .att { position: relative; padding-left: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.5; }
  .att::before { content: ""; position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0.1em; width: 17px; height: 17px; border-radius: 50%; background-repeat: no-repeat; background-position: center; background-size: 10px; }
  .att--ok::before { background-color: #dff0e8; background-image: url(/icons/check.svg); }
  .att--no::before { background-color: #f6dcd2; background-image: url(/icons/x.svg); }
  .att__t { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  .att__d { color: var(--muted); }
  .att__t::after { content: " — "; color: var(--faint); }

  .compliance__row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 12rem 1fr; gap: 0.4rem 1.4rem; padding: 1rem 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .compliance__row:first-child { border-top: none; padding-top: 0; }
  .compliance dt { font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink); }
  .compliance dd { margin: 0; color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.55; }

  .sec-disclosure p { color: var(--muted); line-height: 1.6; max-width: 60ch; }

  @media (max-width: 820px) {
    .mech { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .compliance__row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 0.2rem; }
  }
</style>
